I have everything needed. Here is the complete trace of the POST /api/owners create-owner flow.

## Overview of the create-owner path

The endpoint `POST /api/owners` is declared on the OpenAPI-generated interface `OwnersApi` and implemented by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)`. (`OwnerRestControllerV2` only adds a paginated GET listing; it has no create method.) Validation is layered: Bean Validation on the request DTO (triggered by `@Valid` in the generated interface) runs first; then imperative business-rule checks in `addOwner`; then entity-lifecycle callbacks fire on persist.

---

## 1. The endpoint mapping + Bean Validation trigger (generated interface)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`

The interface is annotated `@Validated` (line 44). The create operation is mapped here:

```java
String PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners";
...
@RequestMapping(
    method = RequestMethod.POST,
    value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,        // "/owners"
    produces = { "application/json" },
    consumes = { "application/json" }
)
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
) { ... default 501 body ... }
```

The `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` is what forces DTO Bean Validation (item 3) to run before the controller body executes. The controller's `@RequestMapping("/api")` (below) + this `/owners` combine to `POST /api/owners`.

---

## 2. The @RestController method (the actual handler)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class header (lines 51-72): `@RestController`, `@CrossOrigin(...)`, `@RequestMapping("/api")`, implements `OwnersApi`; constructor-injects `ClinicService`, `OwnerMapper`, `PetMapper`, `VisitMapper`.

The handler (lines 99-131), guarded by `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")`:

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    owner.setHouseholdId(Households.idFor(owner));
    Collection<Owner> owners = this.clinicService.findAllOwners();
    owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDays.effective(owner));
    if (owners.stream()
        .filter(o -> owner.getRegistrationDate().equals(o.getRegistrationDate())).count() >= 100) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);
    }
    if (Identities.isDuplicate(owners, owner)) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    if (Households.isDuplicate(owners, owner, ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    if (CityCodes.countInCity(owners, owner) >= 50) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    owner.setHouseholdMemberCount(Households.size(owners, owner));
    owner.assignCustomerCode(CityCodes.countInCity(owners, owner));
    owner.setNamesakeCount(Namesakes.count(owners, owner));
    owner.setBulkSignupWarning(BulkSignups.exceededDailyLimit(owners, owner));
    owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(
        PossibleDuplicates.matchId(owners, owner, ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

Exact runtime order inside the handler:
1. Map DTO → `Owner` (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, ignores id/pets).
2. Compute + set `householdId` (`Households.idFor`).
3. Load ALL owners into memory (`clinicService.findAllOwners()`).
4. Default/roll-forward `registrationDate` (`BusinessDays.effective`).
5. Rate-limit: `>=100` owners already on that registration date → `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`.
6. Hard identity duplicate → `409 CONFLICT`.
7. Household duplicate (unless `sharesHousehold==true`) → `409 CONFLICT`.
8. City saturation `>=50` in same city → `409 CONFLICT`.
9. Set `householdMemberCount`, assign `customerCode`, set `namesakeCount`, set `bulkSignupWarning`, set `possibleDuplicateOf`.
10. Persist (`clinicService.saveOwner`).
11. Map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location` header, return `201 CREATED`.

Note: the `Emails` uniqueness helper (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/Emails.java`) exists but is NOT called from `addOwner`; email is only checked by the `@Email`/`@DisposableEmailValidation` DTO constraints.

---

## 3. Service layer

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` (interface) — relevant methods: `Collection<Owner> findAllOwners()` (line 57) and `void saveOwner(Owner owner)` (line 59).

