## 6. Side-effects during creation

- Audit logging (entity lifecycle): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/OwnerAuditListener.java`. Registered via `@EntityListeners` on `Owner`. Its `@PostPersist onCreate(Owner)` (lines 16-21) logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `"AUDIT"` at INFO: `owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=...`. `membershipLevel` is computed by `MembershipLevels.levelOf(owner)`.
  - `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/MembershipLevels.java` — derives points (email +2, no namesakes +1, household>=3 +2, tenure>365d +3) and maps to level 1-4. Called both by the audit listener and by the response mapper.
- Response-mapping computations (not persisted, but computed on the way out): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` `toOwnerDto` derives `displayName`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit` (CheckDigits.luhnOf), `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference` (ContactPreferences), `ageBand` (AgeBands), `telephoneDisplay` (TelephoneDisplays). These helper classes live under `.../mapper/` and `.../rest/controller/v1/`.
- Monitoring aspect: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CallMonitoringAspect.java` — `@Aspect` `@Around("within(@org.springframework.stereotype.Repository *)")` counts calls/time via JMX. NOTE: it only advises classes annotated `@Repository`; `SpringDataOwnerRepository` is not, so (per the class's own comment) it does NOT wrap the owner-save call under the spring-data-jpa profile.
- No event publishing (`publishEvent`/`ApplicationEvent`), no email sending (`JavaMailSender`), no `@Async`, and no caching (`@Cacheable`/`@CacheEvict`) exist anywhere in this path — confirmed by grep across `src/main`. The only "email" logic is the validation blocklist in `DisposableEmailValidator`.

